Terminal pairing and complementary-minor proofs

The new terminal-order, copied-forest transport, determinant-coefficient,
zero-sum bordering and complementary-minor proofs are original to this library.
VertexTransport adapts the repository-local ReflTransGen.lift witness
construction from GroundedTreeNormalization.lean, original SHA256
820d1ba602326c41442c2ba46ae0faed4ece6addcdb00810c068a2840c36d1d2.
The nonground subtype equivalences follow the repository-local constructions
in GroundedTreeNormalization.lean and TerminalGreenInverse.lean. The signed
complement-order proof uses the existing root-column expansion API.
Exact source hashes and prior proof-review commitments are recorded in
LatticeProb/PORT-PROVENANCE.json. These additions retain the library's supplied
Apache-2.0 license; this notice does not create an additional license grant.

Generic finite stacks, loop erasure and local plane topology

The twelve finite-stack, loop-erasure and independent-cell modules listed in
LatticeProb/WILSON-PLANE-PROVENANCE.json are extracted from Scott Armstrong's
finite-avalanches formalization. The original loop-erasure attribution is
retained in its source header. The six local-plane topology modules have the
same source project. Exact source-byte hashes and independent source-port review
commitments are recorded in that file; no source commit is asserted to contain
previously uncommitted mathematical files. Copying and adaptation were
explicitly authorized by the source author. The source checkout supplied no
separate LICENSE; this notice asserts no additional historical license grant.
The destination library's existing LICENSE is unchanged. No new third-party
source payload or package dependency is introduced.
